{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Also</b> — Let him pray to HaShem that He bring about causes, for upon Him designs are formed, that He darken the company of the insolent and their evil from him, and let them not rule over him." "<b>And the sense of then I shall be blameless</b> — Then I shall be blameless, and it is a rare word. And the sense: for he cannot keep the commandments if the insolent rule over him, for they will coerce him."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:52.832064232Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}